{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q338106","formula":"KAl₃(SO₄)₂(OH)₆","hill":"Al3H6KO14S2","elements":["H","O","Al","S","K"],"composition":{"H":6.0,"K":1.0,"O":14.0,"S":2.0,"Al":3.0},"names":{"en":"Alunite","ru":"Алунит","uk":"Алуніт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Alunite is a hydroxylated aluminium potassium sulfate mineral, formula KAl3(SO4)2(OH)6. It was first observed in the 15th century at Tolfa, near Rome, where it was mined for the manufacture of alum. First called aluminilite by J.C. Delamétherie in 1797, this name was contracted by François Beudant three decades later to alunite.","ru":"Алуни́т (фр. alunite), также ала́уншпат, алу́ншпат или квасцо́вый ка́мень — квасцы) — минерал состава K2SO4·Al2(SO4)3·4Al(OH)3 или KAl3(SO4)2(OH)6. Цвет белый, серый.","uk":"Алуні́т або галуняк (від лат. alun — галун, галунний камінь) — мінерал з групи сульфатів, основний сульфат алюмінію та калію острівної будови."},"fame":36,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q338106","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alunite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mineraly.sk_-_alunit_m.jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q3785465","formula":"PbAl₃(SO₄)(AsO₄)(OH)₆","names":{"en":"Hidalgoite"},"elements":["H","O","Al","S","As","Pb"],"fame":7,"kind":null},{"id":"